"answer": "Project Zenith is an initiative aimed at optimizing cloud storage solutions, enhancing security, accessibility, and data visualization through AI and machine learning. The project kicked off in Q3 2023 with Marcus Cole as the leader. Key milestones include the completion of the R&D phase and the transition to prototype development starting January 5, 2024, followed by testing on February 1 and a final presentation on March 15. The project budget was initially approved at $2M, though a later update noted an adjustment to $550,000 due to unforeseen expenses. The team has expanded with new members Mike Chen and Lisa Ray. Initial findings suggest a potential 20% efficiency increase. There are also ongoing discussions about a potential partnership with TechInnovate for AI technology."
